## New-angle scan (found one finding, fixed in this batch)

1. [G2-1 residual — FOUND and FIXED] the round-5 free-text rule refused only
   `ord(ch) < 0x20 or == 0x7F`, but Unicode line separators (U+0085 NEL,
   U+2028, U+2029) sit above that range and still split the value everywhere
   Python splits text (`str.splitlines`): a poisoned `reason` of
   `trusted-value<U+2029>+ BW_ROLE_WORKER=evil-model` passed validation and
   would have rendered the forged diff line in `why bench:`. Empirically
   confirmed against the pre-fix rule, then fixed in
   `ggufbench_store.py::_required_line` — the single-line rule is now
   `value.splitlines() != [value]` → `source_unparseable` ("is not a single
   line"). Regression rows: `reason_forges_via_unicode_line_separator` (bench
   table) and the `reason_forges_via_unicode_line_separator` end-to-end propose
   row; probe over MCP stdio in demo.log (`poisoned-separator` →
   `source_unparseable`, `proposal: ""`, no `- `/`+ ` line in the answer).
2. Token fields (model/task/baseline/engine_build/graded dimension) were
   hardened in the same spot: `\S+` already refuses every Unicode whitespace
   including the line separators (probe p1: `model="a<U+2029>b"` → "not a
   single-line whitespace-free token"), and `_refuse_control_chars` now also
   refuses control characters that are `\S` (probe p2: `model="a<NUL>b"` →
   "contains control characters") so a NUL cannot ride into a proposal or a
   pasted role env.
3. Run-side structure re-checked: step fields are `\S+`/`[^"]*` on one physical
   line, so no run finding can carry a line break; the `task:` header value is
   line-bounded by construction (`splitlines()` before mapping). No new gap.

## Residual probes (all PASS; transient probe, output embedded below)

1. U+2029 in a token → `source_unparseable` "not a single-line whitespace-free
   token"; no forged line in the answer.
2. NUL in a token → `source_unparseable` "contains control characters".
3. U+0085 in `reason` → `source_unparseable` "is not a single line".
4. whitespace-only `reason` → accepted as findings (free text may be blank-ish;
   renders inside a `why …: (…) — …` line it cannot break out of).
5. whitespace-only `model` → token refusal.
6. graded dimension `a:b` → accepted; the rendered `signature:` key is
   ambiguous-looking (`a:b:40@…`) but comparability compares the
   `TaskSignature` dataclasses, never the key, and two genuinely different
   gradings still refuse as `incomparable_rows` (R7 tests) — rendering-only.
7. negative finite score → accepted as findings (ggufbench's `pass` verdict is
   authoritative, ADR-0004 comparability is not re-derived from the score;
   ranking prefers higher scores, and NaN/±Inf/overflow refuse at the score
   boundary from round 2).
8. `run.inspect` pointed at a directory → `run_source_missing` (there is no run
   log at that path; same "non-regular means not-here" direction the bench side
   established for a stray `README.md` under the artifact root).
9. bench_path pointed at a plain `results.json` file → `bench_source_missing`
   (the tool contract promises a run directory or the artifact root).
10. positive control: the clean cohort still renders the pasteable
    `+ BW_ROLE_WORKER=llama-3.1-8b-instruct-q4_k_m` diff unchanged.

## Defended findings (recorded per protocol, no action)

1. PEP 758 unparenthesized `except FileNotFoundError, NotADirectoryError:`
   sits next to parenthesized multi-excepts in the same files (carried G3 nit).
   Defended: valid on the py314 target and `ruff format` normalizes towards the
   unparenthesized shape — hand-parenthesizing would fight the formatter (the
   round-0 scaffold already lost one `harness/tools` file to exactly that).
   The formatter is the canon; homogeneity follows it, not the reverse.
2. Set-but-empty `DEBRIEF_BENCH_ROOT`/`DEBRIEF_RUN_ROOT` degrades to the
   server cwd (carried G3 nit from round 5). Defended: unchanged this round
   (not part of the ordered fix), operator misconfiguration, and an empty root
   still cannot read outside itself — `_resolve_within` keeps every requested
   path relative to whatever root resolves. Candidate for a future batch.
3. Signature-key ambiguity via `:`/`@` inside a graded dimension name
   (probe 6): rendering-only; comparability never reads the key.

